-- DICT-SEMANTICS §3 `inst` / §6 C1 / §6 "uniform resolution" / §10's last-but-one
-- bullet ("Suspect any resolution code path that ... KEYS INSTANCES BY
-- CLASS-PLUS-HEAD-CONSTRUCTOR ALONE, WHICH CANNOT SEPARATE `List Int` FROM
-- `List a`").
--
-- 🚨 PINNED DIVERGENCE -- ⚠️ UNFILED. Reported to the orchestrator on 2026-07-30
-- with this repro and the control below; no open issue matched when this landed.
-- Severity as observed: **S0, silent wrongness** -- `check` exits 0 with no
-- diagnostic and BOTH engines print a value produced by an impl whose head the
-- goal DOES NOT MATCH.
--
-- SPEC ANSWER (hand-derived, before running anything):
--   `match(IE, π)` = { I | ∃φ. φ(head(I)) = π } (§3). `head(impl Tag (Box Int))`
--   is `Box Int`; no substitution makes it `Box String` or `Box Bool`. So:
--     goal `Tag (Box Int)`    -> match {Tag a, Tag (Box Int)}, min⊑ = Box Int => 99
--     goal `Tag (Box String)` -> match {Tag a} ALONE                          => 10
--     goal `Tag (Box Bool)`   -> match {Tag a} ALONE                          => 10
--   Expected output: 99, 10, 10.
--
-- OBSERVED on this binary: **99, 99, 99** -- on `check` (exit 0, no diagnostic),
-- on `run`, and on the shipped native binary alike. Two of the three lines call
-- an impl their goal does not match.
--
-- MECHANISM (read off `medaka build --keep-ir`, not inferred): all three call
-- sites lower to a DIRECT call to `@mdk_impl_Box_tag` -- the mangled symbol for
-- `impl Tag (Box Int)` carries the HEAD TYCON ONLY, with the type ARGUMENTS
-- dropped. Selection is therefore keyed on `Box`, which cannot separate
-- `Box Int` from `Box String`. Because the call is direct, the decision is taken
-- during elaboration, not at run time -- so it is not the runtime arm-matching
-- site of #1072, and #1072 states explicitly that "single-module permutations are
-- CLEAN", which this program contradicts. Treat them as adjacent, not identical,
-- until someone traces both.
--
-- 🔬 THE CONTROL IS IN THE CORPUS, ONE TOKEN AWAY. `s5-argtag-unsound-under-
-- overlap.mdk` is this program with the general sibling written `impl Tag (List a)`
-- instead of `impl Tag a`, and it answers CORRECTLY (99, 10). So the trigger is
-- specifically a FULLY GENERAL instance (a bare type-variable head, which mangles
-- to `__none__` and enters no head bucket) sitting beside a tycon-headed one --
-- not overlap as such, and not declaration order. `test/dict_fixtures/
-- s3-nested-obligation-most-specific.mdk` is a second control at parametric width.
--
-- ⚠️ THIS ROW PINS A WRONG ANSWER ON PURPOSE, AND THE VALUE IT PINS IS NOT
-- CORRECT. Do not "confirm" it against the engines -- they are the thing that is
-- wrong. It goes RED the day selection starts keying on the full head, which is
-- the signal to re-pin it to the spec answer `99\n10\n10` and close the issue
-- this becomes.
data Box a = Box a

interface Tag a where
  tag : a -> Int

impl Tag a where
  tag _ = 10

impl Tag (Box Int) where
  tag _ = 99

main =
  println (tag (Box (1 : Int)))
  println (tag (Box "s"))
  println (tag (Box True))
